# 2026-09-14: aliases for hull-consuming sub-units that had no entity of ANY kind - neither an
# alias here nor a native declaration in a <TAG>_unit.asset / *_units_*.asset file - and so fell
# back to a default battlefield model.
#
# Coverage is alias-or-native: armored_infantry, mechanized_airborne, mechanized_marine and a
# few mechanized_infantry entries already have per-country entities, so NOTHING is declared for
# them here. This file carries the zz_ prefix and therefore loads last, so an alias for one of
# those names would override a national model with a generic one.
#
# Clone target follows what the sub-unit fields: troop carriers take mechanized_entity
# (units_vehicles.asset:50), the marine variant mechanized_marine_entity (:68). Armour-based
# support clones the entity that TAG already uses for the matching armour family, and
# spaag_support clones that TAG's own spaag entity where it has one.
#
# Levels are the consumed hull's visual_level ceiling plus one: 10 for APC and the light and
# medium tank hulls, 8 for IFV, 5 for light AA and heavy.

